 "notes": "All geometry from the Electric Herald 1:1 vector templates; the front view is a true front view (rhythm plate and longer horn on bass/-x side, tuners on bass edge, low-E post nearest the nut). Body is 35.11 x 48.71 cm overall (13.82 x 19.18in); on the centreline the body runs y=0..44.64. The lowest point of the whole body (y=-0.55) is off-centre on the treble side (x=+6.96), so some outline points have y<0. BODY OUTLINE INCLUDES THE NECK-POCKET NOTCH: across the neck the outline follows the pocket mouth at y=44.64 (flush with where the bass-side edge meets the neck), then runs down the treble side of the pocket at x=+2.74 to y=40.40 where the treble cutaway starts; the neck heel fills this notch. Neck: nut (fretboard side) at body y=83.82, fret n at nutY - 64.77*(1-2^(-n/12)); fretboard/neck end and pocket end at y=37.03; neck width 4.19 cm at nut, 5.16 cm at 12th, 5.55 cm at 21st fret. Neck plate (back) 5.08 x 6.40 cm centred on x=0, y=41.18; neck screws at x=+-1.91, y=43.72 and 38.64. Bridge post centres are 0.12 cm behind the scale line (saddleLineY=19.05). Pickguard outline includes the neck-heel cutout (follows the heel arc) and passes around the rhythm plate; the rhythm plate sits in a matching cutout. Knob positions are control-hole centres (hole 0.95 cm); vintage JM knobs are ~1.9 cm dia (estimated). Jack is pickguard-mounted on the lower treble side. Headstock is the original 1958-67 Jazzmaster headstock (19.57 cm long from the nut, larger than a pre-CBS Strat's ~18.6 cm), not the Strat shape; outline closed straight across the nut line y=0. String tree (B/high-e) at headstock [1.41, 7.44]. Truss rod adjusts at the heel (no headstock cover). Contour depths are estimates (JM contours are shallower than a Strat's)."
